{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-106661",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "An inhibited growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=k(a-y),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>y$ for all $t\\ge 0.$\n\nFrom the given options, the only inhibited growth equation is\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dt}=0.5(150-y).\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.5,$ and $a=150.$ Note that for inhibited growth, we must have $y<150$ for all $t\\ge 0.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
